course: dictionary
lesson: 2062
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can often tell which meaning is right by reading the words around it, which are its context. «Stoats held the conservatory, the billiard-room and the French windows onto the lawn.» The other rooms are part of a house, so the conservatory must be a room too.
explain: Read the clues. A conservatory is a room with glass walls and a glass roof, built onto a house. People sit there in the sun and grow plants. In a big park or garden, a conservatory can also be a large glass building for tender plants, which is like a greenhouse.
explain: The word can also mean a school for musicians. «A gifted violinist may study at a conservatory.» Violinists do not study in a glass room full of plants, so the clue is gifted violinist, and the meaning is a college for training musicians.
fact: A conservatory is a room with glass walls and a glass roof, built onto a house.
fact: In a garden or park, a conservatory is a big glass building for growing tender plants, a bit like a greenhouse.
fact: In science, a conservatory works like a greenhouse: sunlight comes through the glass and warms the air, so plants keep growing.
fact: A conservatoire, also spelled conservatory, is a school or college for training musicians, singers or actors.
fact: When a word has more than one meaning, read the sentence to find the right one.
exercise: «Stoats held the conservatory, the billiard-room and the French windows onto the lawn.» Which kind of place is a conservatory here? | A cellar full of wine barrels | A tall tower on a castle wall | A river that runs past the garden | *A room with glass walls and a glass roof, joined to the house
exercise: Mum says the plants must go in the conservatory to keep warm. How does the glass help them? | It turns the plants into stone | *It lets sunlight in and warms the air, like a greenhouse | It keeps all light out so the plants can sleep | It makes the air cold and wet
exercise: A gifted violinist goes to a conservatory. What is a conservatory here? | A glass room for sitting in the sun | A kitchen for cooking | *A school or college for training musicians | A park full of tender plants
test: «Weasels crept up the carriage-drive to the front door.» What does crept suggest? | Danced in the rain | Ran loudly and quickly | *Moved slowly and quietly | Flew over the wall
test: Which word from the Wild Wooders sentences means a room with glass walls, where people sit in the sun? | Kitchen-garden | Lawn | Billiard-room | *Conservatory
exam: Ella reads «The conservatory was full of ferns and palms.» Using the clues, what is a conservatory here? | A bedroom with a bed of ferns | A shop that sells ferns | *A glass room or greenhouse full of plants | A river with palms on its banks
